@node jQuery API
@chapter jQuery API
@anchor{#jquery-api}
jQuery is a fast, small, and feature-rich JavaScript library. It makes
things like HTML document traversal and manipulation, event handling,
animation, and Ajax much simpler with an easy-to-use API that works
across a multitude of browsers. If you're new to jQuery, we recommend
that you check out the @uref{https://learn.jquery.com/,jQuery Learning
Center}.

If you're updating to a newer version of jQuery, be sure to read the
release notes published on @uref{https://blog.jquery.com/,our blog}. If
you're coming from a version prior 1.9, you should check out the
@uref{https://jquery.com/upgrade-guide/1.9/,1.9 Upgrade Guide} as well.

Note that this is the API documentation for jQuery core. Other projects
have API docs in other locations:

@itemize
@item
@uref{https://api.jqueryui.com/,jQuery UI API docs}
@item
@uref{https://api.jquerymobile.com/,jQuery Mobile API docs}
@item
@uref{https://api.qunitjs.com/,QUnit API docs}
@end itemize

